## XLivelessAddon (original)

The launcher/SecuROM bypass, the save/settings path redirects, the WM_ROM message
window, the borderless window handling and the INI layout descend from
[XLivelessAddon](https://github.com/GTAmodding/XLivelessAddon) by the GTAmodding
community, released into the public domain. `source/skip_launcher.ixx`,
`source/skip_launcher_recovered.inc`, `source/rom_window.ixx`,
`source/savegames.ixx` and `source/windowed.ixx` carry a header that attributes
the bodies.

## ZolikaPatch

The recovered signature tables, the SkipLauncher stage split (main, DFA, ROM),
the DFA file-API hooks and the legacy launcher stage are a reimplementation of
the machine-level behaviour of ZolikaPatch 7.65 by Zolika1351. ZolikaPatch shipped
as a compiled ASI without source; no original source is redistributed here.

## GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix

The borderless-window/focus-loss logic (`source/windowed.ixx`), the
SHGetFolderPath user-data redirect (`source/profile.ixx`) and the shared
`Event`, `Log`, `Game` and `find_pattern` shapes (`source/common.ixx`) follow
GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix (`windowed.ixx`, `userdata.ixx`, `common.ixx`), Copyright
(C) ThirteenAG and contributors, GPL-3.0. The windowed compatibility gates in
`source/config.ixx` follow the same project's approach. The local-directory
options are deliberately **not** gated on FusionFix being present.

## Vendored libraries (committed, not submodules)

The licence text of each library is committed next to it. The libraries are
compiled from these pinned copies only; nothing is fetched at build time.

| Path | Project | Revision | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `external/injector` | [ThirteenAG/injector](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/injector) (LINK/2012) | `fdd277056a9b12e209d58c35a269277391cf955a` | zlib |
| `external/hooking` | [ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns) (NTAuthority, CitizenFX) | `460a47bc813085b66c79768531caab1ed5ea96fc` | MIT |
| `external/inireader` | [ThirteenAG/IniReader](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/IniReader) | `206c4b343d3cb0d2ca83afd1fccbe71331137a37` | MIT |
| `external/inireader/mINI` | [metayeti/mINI](https://github.com/metayeti/mINI) (Danijel Durakovic) | bundled by the above | MIT |

The pinned injector is the classic 2017 tree. Its `MakeRET` stores
`pop ? 0xC2 : 0xC3` through a deduced `int`, so it writes four bytes for both
`ret` forms; the maintained fork fixed this, but this tree keeps the requested
classic pin and `source/patch.ixx` writes `ret`/`ret N` itself at the exact
one-/three-byte width. The vendored header is unmodified.

The pinned `CIniReader` is all-inline; MSVC 19.51's CL.exe crashes when a
function body that instantiates it is imported into another module interface
unit. The tree keeps the reader inside `source/config.ixx` and makes
`config::Load`/`config::Publish` out-of-line, so `source/dllmain.cpp` remains the
only plain TU. The reader is unmodified.

## Game assets

Grand Theft Auto IV and Episodes from Liberty City are property of Rockstar Games
and Take-Two Interactive. This repository ships no game executables, archives,
textures or other game data. It only writes to memory of a game the user already
owns.
